# Controls what `gcloud run deploy --source`/`gcloud builds submit` uploads
# to Cloud Build — a separate, earlier step than the Docker build itself.
# Deliberately NOT derived from .gitignore (gcloud's default when this file
# is absent): .gitignore excludes data/video/* (correctly, for git — that
# media should never be committed), but the orchestrator's vision agents read
# video frames directly off local disk at runtime (tools/video_utils.py::
# _find_source_video, no GCS fallback) — confirmed live: deploying with the
# auto-derived .gcloudignore made every case fail with "no source video found
# for 'video_01'" because the file never even reached Cloud Build, let alone
# the image. data/video/ and data/annotations/ (used by the benchmark agent's
# ground-truth comparison) are intentionally left uploadable here.

.venv/
.uv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.git/
.github/

node_modules/
ui/frontend/dist/
ui/frontend/.vite/

data/mri/
data/runtime/

.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.key.json
service-account*.json

*.log
